# Windows safety. This repo's own tools rewrite these files byte-for-byte
# (sync-version.mjs, apply-unnerfs.py) and every un-nerf rule matches its prompt
# by an exact text anchor, so the on-disk form has to be LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true checks out *.sh with
# CRLF — bash then dies on the shebang — and a regenerated prompt set shows all
# ~6,900 files as modified even when the bytes are identical.
* text=auto eol=lf
